,"requests":10}}],"version":1},"findings":[{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] State how the three external client CLIs (copilot/codex/claude) are provisioned (or shimmed/skipped) within the hermetic `make test`, so the server-list and read-tool oracles are actually executable; if a client binary is unavailable, define the fallback (e.g. structural config-shape validation) that still proves the config is accepted.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"assert via each client's server-list command: `copilot mcp get rebar`, `codex mcp list`, `claude mcp list`\"","\"drives a real read-tool call through each resolved client config\"","The plan's hermetic test only 'spins up an in-process/loopback `rebar-mcp` HTTP server'; nothing establishes presence of the copilot/codex/claude CLIs in the test environment (ABSENCE in plan text).","tests/interfaces/facades/ contains rebar-side MCP tests but no evidence of third-party client CLI harnessing."],"finding":"The acceptance/proof mechanism drives real third-party client CLIs (copilot/codex/claude) for its server-list and read-tool oracles, but the plan only spins up the in-repo loopback rebar-mcp server and never states how those external client binaries are made available in the hermetic `make test` run — leaving the central oracle potentially unexecutable in CI.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f50df4da9bd204aae","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria (server-list oracle: `copilot mcp get rebar`, `codex mcp list`, `claude mcp list`) + Testing/Verification (proof command)","norm_id":"n993a65b333e567f3","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["CI or a fresh dev box where copilot/codex/claude CLIs are not installed — the server-list and read-tool oracles cannot run and the proof command fails or silently no-ops.","A reviewer/implementer must decide whether to shell out to real CLIs vs. parse/validate the config shapes structurally, with no guidance."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a subsection to Testing/Verification specifying, per client, either (a) the CLI is a documented test prerequisite and the test skips-with-reason when absent, or (b) a client-agnostic structural loader validates each committed example config against the client's documented schema and the loopback rebar-mcp handles the resolved bearer request — keeping the 401 contrast and the real-tool-result assertions on the parts that don't require the external binary.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"medium"}}},{"block_threshold":0.9,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Cite the observed source (client version + `--help`/docs) for each asserted client surface: codex `bearer_token_env_var`, copilot `type:http`/`headers`/`$VAR`, claude `.mcp.json`/`${VAR}`/`--transport http --header`, and the three server-list subcommands — or classify each as Unverified pending a spike.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'Research confirmed all three clients support a static Authorization: Bearer <PAT> header ... none require OAuth'","Plan asserts codex `bearer_token_env_var = \"MCP_CLIENT_PAT_CODEX\"` and copilot `$VAR`/claude `${VAR}` expansion as fact","In-repo .codex/config.toml demonstrates only [mcp_servers.serena] with a stdio `command`, NOT an HTTP entry with `bearer_token_env_var` — the asserted HTTP+bearer key surface is unconfirmed in-repo","ADR 0104 (docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md) does not document any of the asserted client config keys or CLI subcommands","Evidence class: Partially-verified / Unverified — the integration category exists but the specific per-client surface is not observed"],"finding":"The client-side external surfaces the plan depends on — codex TOML key `bearer_token_env_var`, copilot `type: http` + `headers` map with `$VAR` expansion, claude `.mcp.json` `type: http` + `${VAR}` and `claude mcp add --transport http --header`, plus the three server-list oracles `copilot mcp get rebar` / `codex mcp list` / `claude mcp list` — are asserted as 'research confirmed' but with no citable source (client version, `--help` output, or docs URL). These are key/flag-level surfaces where a name mismatch fails silently at runtime.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f952add3cf055524d","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach + rationale ('research-confirmed static bearer for all three'); Acceptance Criteria (server-list oracles)","norm_id":"n194cc5e657f79c6a","priority":0.7,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A codex key that is actually named differently (e.g. not `bearer_token_env_var`) is silently ignored, so no Authorization header is sent and the request 401s or connects unauthenticated","`copilot mcp get rebar` or `codex mcp list` is not the actual subcommand, so the acceptance oracle cannot be run as written"],"severity":"critical